## Define Compute Image for Provisioning

### Build Initial Base OS Image

The following steps build a minimal, default image for use with xCAT. A local
copy of the distribution ISO is required; for this recipe the ISO is
`{{ distro_iso_image }}`. Initialize image creation using `copycds`, assuming
the ISO is available at `${iso_path}`:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Initialize OS images for use with xCAT -->
```bash
: "${iso_path:?ERROR: iso_path not set}"

copycds ${iso_path}/{{ distro_iso_image }}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

`copycds` derives the OS image names from the distribution metadata inside the
ISO, which encodes the minor version (for example a Rocky 10.0 x86_64 ISO
creates `rocky10.0-x86_64-{install,netboot,statelite}-compute`). Query the
created images and capture the stateless (*netboot*) image name for the
following steps:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Capture the netboot osimage name created by copycds -->
```bash
# Query available images
lsdef -t osimage

# Capture the stateless (netboot) compute image name
xcat_osimage=$(lsdef -t osimage | awk '/netboot-compute/{print $1; exit}')
echo ${xcat_osimage}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

This recipe uses the stateless (*netboot*) image. Proceed by running `genimage`
to initialize a chroot-based install:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Create chroot-based compute image -->
```bash
# Save chroot location for the compute image
CHROOT=$(lsdef -t osimage -o ${xcat_osimage} \
    -i rootimgdir | awk -F= '/rootimgdir/{print $2}')/rootimg/
export CHROOT

# Build initial chroot image
genimage ${xcat_osimage}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
